1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
Hello Hello!

2
00:00:02,603 --> 00:00:06,652
We are in Hammarby Sjöstad in Stockholm, and what should we do?

3
00:00:06,885 --> 00:00:09,341
- Bake!
- Yay!

4
00:00:09,475 --> 00:00:16,168
A while ago we got an email from a guy named Albin.
His father is a baker and is called Magnus.

5
00:00:16,345 --> 00:00:18,555
His bakery & pastry is there!

6
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:20,537
Here!

7
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:26,740
- They should teach us to bake.
- Hopefully something very miserable.

8
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:36,720
We will bake pastries and croissants.

9
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:41,900
- Yes!
I love croissants.
And pastry.
- It will be super good.

10
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:09,580
- How big will they be?
- It depends on how big you make them.

11
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,980
What did you say?

12
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:15,620
- 1044 layers exactly?
- Stay here.
No Harry, absolutely not!

13
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:19,820
- May I count them?
- Yes, you have to do that when we eat them.

14
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:26,020
We have rolled so, and then we turn it in this direction, and we will do the same again.

15
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:29,780
- Who is going to drive now, then?
- Alma!
Alma, beware!

16
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:33,800
Now we must be careful so that we do not destroy the layers.
Okay Alma, then we press here.

17
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:56,800
- Pull a little in the dough too.
- Good.

18
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,840
A little more.

19
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,000
Good.

20
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:06,360
Now these are going to ferment for about an hour and a half.

21
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:07,860
Okay.

22
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:09,680
- Sad, huh?
- Yes.

23
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:13,860
- Then we have to sit and roll our thumbs.
- It's lucky that I have ice cream then, right?

24
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:15,580
Yes!

25
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:20,060
Albin will ask today's question when eating ice cream.

26
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:25,100
"What countries have Alma and Harry been in?"

27
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:28,680
Good question.
Do you remember?

28
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,620
Yes!

29
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:57,160
- What a good bill.
We have never counted ourselves.
- No, but I think it's actually true.

30
00:07:57,260 --> 00:08:01,460
Move some Harry, so Alma comes out.

31
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:06,580
Here comes the Tuffe-Tuffe train!

32
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:10,240
TUT-TUT!

33
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:12,260
TUT-TUT!

34
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,340
They crashed.

35
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,580
TUT-TUT-TUT!
Pang!

36
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:20,880
- In the middle of the cake.
- Stylish holes.
